&lt;h5 style="color: #4fc3f7; margin-bottom: 0.4rem;"&gt;What Does This Mean?&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem; color: #cfd8dc;"&gt;
  Achieving &lt;strong&gt;9.43% accuracy&lt;/strong&gt; on 23 classes is statistically significant ($p &lt; 0.0001$), proving that musical genres have real, measurable visual conventions. Simple color and brightness statistics contain more than double the information of random chance.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-bottom: 0; color: #cfd8dc;"&gt;
  At the same time, the fact that accuracy remains under 10% proves that &lt;strong&gt;album cover artwork is not a rigid barcode&lt;/strong&gt;. While Disco tends toward neon saturation and Metal leans into darkness, artists within every genre actively explore diverse aesthetics. Music has a visual identity, but it is nuanced, artistic, and multifaceted.
&lt;/p&gt;
